{"w":2400,"h":3390,"lines":[{"h":0.017046585758175525,"c":1,"w":0.064397691090901696,"x":0.081740947930612276,"y":0.044150577631855259,"t":"Test 1"},{"c":1,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","w":0.31211499532063802,"x":0.082135520717504379,"y":0.091445427461028128,"h":0.017699115044247815},{"h":0.024080399144715603,"y":0.12699381063822468,"x":0.081979771289098557,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","w":0.82576919555664063,"c":1},{"h":0.018957947137433151,"c":1,"w":0.17453798929850262,"t":"Passage 2 below.","x":0.080082134787533663,"y":0.14534883757155204},{"t":"The pirates of the ancient Mediterranean","y":0.19174041255515151,"w":0.61396306355794272,"h":0.024829354750371624,"c":1,"x":0.19301846808641773},{"y":0.23167762717267804,"t":"In the first and second millennia BCE, pirates sailed around","h":0.020673422124181884,"x":0.2175382865383699,"c":1,"w":0.56285781860351558},{"x":0.22587270088065395,"w":0.5482545979817709,"t":"the Mediterranean, attacking ships and avoiding pursuers","y":0.24999999983806909,"h":0.020348837523333829,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.019580285176414969,"t":"When one mentions pirates, an image springs to most people's minds of a crew of misfits,","x":0.1272489720872996,"y":0.28627458327986788,"w":0.77014633178710945},{"c":1,"x":0.12731006727068556,"w":0.7823408508300782,"y":0.30523255816286343,"t":"daredevils and adventurers in command of a tall sailing ship in the Caribbean Sea. Yet from","h":0.017481305957895543},{"y":0.32267441862634816,"t":"the first to the third millennium BCE, thousands of years before these swashbucklers began","w":0.78234085083007809,"x":0.12525667910925942,"h":0.01744357533862817,"c":1},{"w":0.76796712239583331,"y":0.34011627892151819,"h":0.017441860412777732,"x":0.125256690218921,"c":1,"t":"spreading fear across the Caribbean, pirates prowled the Mediterranean, raiding merchant"},{"y":0.35899704993565373,"t":"ships and threatening vital trade routes. However, despite all efforts and the might of","x":0.1252566838013533,"w":0.7268993631998697,"h":0.017456438407785435,"c":1},{"y":0.37490596563995093,"t":"various ancient states, piracy could not be stopped. The situation remained unchanged for","x":0.12519258267351774,"w":0.76809560139973954,"h":0.020479394693290187,"c":1},{"w":0.7802874755859377,"x":0.12525667277854485,"t":"thousands of years. Only when the pirates directly threatened the interests of ancient Rome","c":1,"h":0.017531899646320293,"y":0.3938053096265941},{"h":0.016224188790560423,"c":1,"y":0.41268436563570343,"w":0.79055440266927079,"x":0.12731006755653501,"t":"did the Roman Republic organise a massive fleet to eliminate piracy. Under the command of"},{"c":1,"y":0.43008849538949367,"h":0.017699115044247815,"t":"the Roman general Pompey, Rome eradicated piracy, transforming the Mediterranean into","x":0.12525666609956981,"w":0.77002054850260415},{"w":0.2340862274169922,"x":0.12731006937158601,"h":0.016020957699215965,"t":"'Mare Nostrum' (Our Sea).","y":0.44622093019043618,"c":1},{"h":0.015988371857499684,"t":"Although piracy in the Mediterranean is first recorded in ancient Egypt during the reign","x":0.12525667815806665,"c":1,"y":0.48401162802248032,"w":0.74948664347330729},{"t":"of Pharaoh Amenhotep III (c 1390-1353 BCE), it is reasonable to assume it predated this","y":0.50145348848765259,"h":0.015988371857499573,"x":0.12525667868344623,"w":0.76591374715169258,"c":1},{"w":0.76603220621744794,"c":1,"t":"powerful civilisation. This is partly due to the great importance the Mediterranean held at","x":0.12520014851201969,"y":0.51835588719831549,"h":0.018972260691774934},{"c":1,"w":0.78234085083007809,"t":"this time, and partly due to its geography. While the Mediterranean region is predominantly","x":0.12525668462089509,"y":0.53628318557034615,"h":0.017495883952903135},{"c":1,"x":0.12518944685317962,"y":0.55383666435221457,"t":"fertile, some parts are rugged and hilly, even mountainous. In the ancient times, the","w":0.71265263875325524,"h":0.018933645602876026},{"c":1,"w":0.77002054850260426,"y":0.57256637154768175,"h":0.017549907493028649,"t":"inhabitants of these areas relied heavily on marine resources, including fish and salt. Most","x":0.12525666607295638},{"c":1,"h":0.018709388665393401,"x":0.12518646929445082,"t":"had their own boats, possessed good seafaring skills, and unsurpassed knowledge of the","y":0.5900486755410238,"w":0.75165781656901043},{"w":0.78028747558593747,"h":0.017515606725462041,"x":0.12525667165261647,"c":1,"y":0.60755813934302971,"t":"local coastline and sailing routes. Thus, it is not surprising that during hardships, these men"},{"t":"turned to piracy. Geography itself further benefited the pirates, with the numerous coves","x":0.12525666555450016,"h":0.016024387550916619,"c":1,"y":0.62645348848687199,"w":0.75359344482421875},{"x":0.12525666586699497,"t":"along the coast providing places for them to hide their boats and strike undetected. Before","y":0.64389534894789657,"h":0.015988371857499684,"w":0.77002054850260415,"c":1},{"t":"the invention of ocean-going caravels\" in the 15th century, ships could not easily cross long","h":0.025011927961951508,"c":1,"w":0.78264699300130225,"x":0.12513395520394804,"y":0.65529367271450267},{"y":0.67876106194067343,"w":0.75770019531250021,"h":0.0174598682594862,"t":"distances over open water. Thus, in the ancient world most were restricted to a few well-","c":1,"x":0.12525667825677439},{"x":0.12518575331983528,"w":0.77426823933919275,"h":0.019545322744543903,"c":1,"t":"known navigable routes that followed the coastline. Caught in a trap, a slow merchant ship","y":0.6959952490244089},{"w":0.76810475667317712,"t":"laden with goods had no other option but to surrender. In addition, knowledge of the local","h":0.018424434155489444,"c":1,"x":0.12517684746156268,"y":0.7146556717006407},{"h":0.016076696165191806,"w":0.57905543009440108,"t":"area helped the pirates to avoid retaliation once a state fleet arrived.","y":0.73392330371395986,"x":0.12525667910738225,"c":1},{"y":0.7601744183410174,"t":"One should also add that it was not unknown in the first and second millennia BCE for","x":0.12525668431567216,"w":0.7433264668782551,"c":1,"h":0.013081395872223012},{"x":0.12519822561761335,"t":"governments to resort to pirates' services, especially during wartime, employing their","y":0.77545423211609155,"h":0.01998661682669034,"c":1,"w":0.73113199869791656},{"y":0.7949852507079137,"x":0.12525666582035636,"h":0.017514749262536822,"t":"skills and numbers against their opponents. A pirate fleet would serve in the first wave of","c":1,"w":0.76180699666341156},{"w":0.77412729899088528,"h":0.017531042183394963,"c":1,"y":0.81386430662498621,"x":0.12525667894053916,"t":"attack, preparing the way for the navy. Some of the regions were known for providing safe"},{"w":0.53593429565429684,"c":1,"y":0.83126843646556603,"h":0.017699115044247704,"x":0.12525667123109316,"t":"harbours to pirates, who, in return, boosted the local economy."},{"w":0.4867851765950521,"x":0.080007402656663132,"y":0.89676788287114717,"h":0.012826459879017205,"c":1,"t":"* caravel: a small, highly manoeuvrable sailing ship developed by the Portuguese"},{"h":0.013081394746943587,"c":1,"x":0.078028748179176335,"t":"20","w":0.026694043477376306,"y":0.92005813977636952},{"c":1,"w":0.45882354736328124,"x":0.51176469619230891,"y":0.94166666659226195,"h":0.04166666666666663,"t":"IELTSXpress.com"}]}